:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.21.0</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated vanilla to 0.5.12.8</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated DoLP to v0.775</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Wren to the pub gambling ring</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wren can now appear at the pub dice table during dusk and night once the gambling ring is running.</li>
		<li>They are more likely to appear while the bank heist is waiting for the player to find them.</li>
		<li>Wren can be met here for the first time, continue the bank heist quest, or be chatted with through several new scenes.</li>
		<li>Once per day, <strong>Ask Wren to read the table</strong> gives a 10% Luck bonus for dice.</li>
		<li>The bonus stacks with other Luck effects and appears as <strong>Wren's Read</strong> in the Traits menu.</li>
		<li>Landry now points the player towards Wren at the gambling ring, with dialogue and Journal hints changing based on whether the ring is open, funded, or not yet funded.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Restored Silly Pregnancy Mode</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Silly Pregnancy Mode can again be selected at character creation or in Pregnancy Mode settings.</li>
		<li>Holding hands or kissing can cause pregnancy instead of sex.</li>
		<li>Direct skin contact is required: gloves block hand-holding pregnancy and face coverings block kissing pregnancy.</li>
		<li>Being near someone the player loves doubles the chance.</li>
		<li>The <strong>Base Player Pregnancy Chance</strong> slider controls the chance in this mode.</li>
		<li><strong>Hail Mary</strong> is disabled while Silly mode is active.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy cannot occur during dreams, flashbacks, or replays.</li>
		<li>Strangers who cannot be met again can no longer become pregnant.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy notices now display correctly for both the player and the other person.</li>
		<li>Restored the missing Silly-mode divider in settings.</li>
		<li>Older saves automatically moved to Fetishised mode remain there unless Silly is selected again.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added the X-Change Gray Agent trait</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>A VrelCoin feat boost that prevents forced pills from changing the player's sex.</li>
		<li>Forced pills behave like gray pills: other effects still apply, but they cannot swap sex or give both sets of genitals.</li>
		<li>Pills taken willingly are unaffected.</li>
		<li>Forced Choice pills still apply the Choice agent.</li>
		<li>Protects against forced pilling from spikes, laced drinks, combat, school, Remy, Avery, prison, mansion events, and similar routes.</li>
		<li>Spike scenes now only describe a body change when one actually happens.</li>
		<li>Also fixes incorrect transformation text when another pill effect is already active.</li>
		<li>The feat boost costs 75 coins.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added configurable body sizes for pilled bodies</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Character-creation size sliders can now use their full range.</li>
		<li>X-Change settings now allow separate breast, ass, and penis size limits for pilled bodies.</li>
		<li>These limits apply the next time a pill creates or restores that body.</li>
		<li>Natural growth and Gender Identity drift also respect these limits.</li>
		<li>Size-changing pills now build from the selected limits instead of jumping straight to maximum size.</li>
		<li>Physical body-part limits still cannot be exceeded.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a Chastity Acclimated trait toggle</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Chastity Acclimated</strong> can now be enabled or disabled under <strong>Settings &gt; X-Change &gt; Traits</strong>.</li>
		<li>Disabling it removes the trait and restores normal frustration from unwanted chastity.</li>
		<li>Re-enabling it keeps previously earned progress and restores the trait if it had already been unlocked.</li>
		<li>Also fixes modded trait settings sometimes failing to apply correctly to existing saves.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added two new ways to remove shackles</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Police can remove shackles in the back workshop in exchange for money and sex.</li>
		<li>Players with Landry's Lockpick Lawyer training set and SSS Skulduggery can pick the shackles themselves in their room.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a second job for Robin at the Ocean Breeze</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>After the player has worked at the cafe, Robin can be recommended to Sam for a two-week weekday-afternoon trial.</li>
		<li>Robin works from 5 PM to 7 PM on school days while the drink stand remains a weekend job.</li>
		<li>The storyline develops over several weeks, including a difficult first shift and a rude-customer event.</li>
		<li>Letting Robin handle the rude customer personally grants the confidence needed for later progress.</li>
		<li>Robin eventually chooses whether to stay on the cafe rota or return to the stand full time.</li>
		<li>The player can encourage either option or leave the choice to Robin.</li>
		<li>Cafe wages go into the same savings tin for Robin as drink-stand earnings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added serving outfits for Robin</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Maid, butler, and waiting outfits can be folded at the wardrobe and carried in a bag.</li>
		<li>A full serving outfit uses one POCKET slot and is physically removed from the wardrobe while packed.</li>
		<li>The outfit can be given to Robin once they work at the cafe.</li>
		<li>Robin's reaction depends on the outfit, their confidence, and whether it involves crossdressing.</li>
		<li>Traumatised Robin refuses the outfit.</li>
		<li>Crossdressing outfits require the normal crossdressing arc to have started.</li>
		<li>A shy Robin may keep an outfit without wearing it until their confidence improves.</li>
		<li>Added new shift scenes for Robin's first day wearing the outfit and the town's later reaction.</li>
		<li>If Robin returns to the stand, they can wear the outfit there instead.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added hair extensions at the hairdresser</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Hair can now be lengthened with extensions for the same price as a normal haircut.</li>
		<li>Longer options are marked <strong>(extensions)</strong>.</li>
		<li>Fringe now has a <strong>Very long</strong> length option.</li>
		<li>Also fixed two-tone preview colours and previews sometimes showing hair slightly longer than the selected length.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Water Dragon reactions for Sydney</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sydney now reacts to the Water Dragon transformation.</li>
		<li>The Water Dragon tail is included in the scene.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added hypno brooding for Gwylan hypnosis</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added antidepressant prescription collection</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The pharmacy now recognises active antidepressant prescriptions from Dr Harper.</li>
		<li>Harper's prescription bundle provides 10 free doses including the antidepressant.</li>
		<li>Expiry dates and collection dialogue are handled correctly.</li>
		<li>The same prescription cannot be collected twice.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added demon transformation skin colours</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Full Demon transformation now changes skin colour based on tan: blue when pale, purple in the middle, and red when fully tanned.</li>
		<li>The mirror can lock one colour or disable the effect.</li>
		<li>Normal skin returns when the transformation ends.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon skin takes priority while active, with Demon skin returning afterward.</li>
		<li>Also fixes transformation skin colours overwriting the player's real skin colour and normal bodies receiving Water Dragon skin from pills.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Avery's after-school pickup destinations</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Mansion residents can ask Avery for a lift to 13 locations, including home, the orphanage, and major town streets.</li>
		<li>Non-residents retain the original orphanage destination.</li>
		<li>Robin, crime, and Rage events are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Virginity statistics now record when virginity is lost while Heat</strong> controls the player's actions.
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Improved fishing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The secret coastal path now has roughly twice the normal bite chance.</li>
		<li>Added the <strong>Bare Bones</strong> feat for catching every small-fish type and finding both Bone tackle pieces.</li>
		<li>Small bass, herring, and trout now record and display correctly when kept.</li>
		<li>Small fish no longer count toward bait-shop requests for their larger species.</li>
		<li>Fish kept after fox or drunk-fisher encounters now count toward active requests.</li>
		<li>Fishing catch names now correctly match the fish caught, including small fish.</li>
		<li>Harpies far enough into their transformation can eat worms without disgust or Trauma and gain 1 Bird point once per day.</li>
		<li>Worms can be eaten from either a worm tin or a shop-bought pack.</li>
		<li>Banish Tentacle is now available during fishing encounters.</li>
		<li>Intentional-loss endings no longer lead to broken fishing encounter states.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved the hairstyle menu on mobile</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The hairstyle grid now adapts to smaller screens instead of always forcing five columns.</li>
		<li>Long hairstyle names no longer stretch the menu or push content off-screen.</li>
		<li>Preview sprites no longer overflow into neighbouring tiles, including with high-resolution art.</li>
		<li>Hairstyle previews are cached and reused instead of being fully rerendered when changing pages or reopening the menu.</li>
		<li>Page switching and reopening the hairstyle menu should now be faster.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved tooltips on mobile and narrow screens</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Tooltips no longer jump to the top of the screen on phones, tablets, or narrow windows.</li>
		<li>They now stay near the hovered or tapped option and move only as needed to remain visible.</li>
		<li>Wide-screen behaviour is unchanged.</li>
		<li>Fixed trait tooltips becoming extremely narrow or running off-screen in landscape mode.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Reorganised X-Change settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Renamed <strong>Talents Settings</strong> to <strong>Talents &amp; Traits</strong>.</li>
		<li>Moved Traits, Willpower System, Hypnosis Settings, and Heat System into this tab.</li>
		<li><strong>X-Change Settings</strong> now focuses on pills, body customisation, combat pilling, and fertility.</li>
		<li>Trait settings now have their own section instead of being hidden under Appearance.</li>
		<li>Related sub-settings now grey out correctly when their parent option is disabled.</li>
		<li>Existing saves, presets, and exported settings are unaffected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Tempered skills now retain SSS progress</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Disabling a Tempered talent or importing mismatched talent choices no longer permanently drops an affected skill back to S.</li>
		<li>Earned SSS progress remains stored.</li>
		<li>Without the required Tempered talent, further progress pauses until the talent is restored.</li>
		<li>Applies to skills, combat skills, school subjects, Physique, Willpower, and Beauty.</li>
		<li>Characteristics and cheat displays now show the retained value correctly.</li>
		<li>Values already lost in older versions cannot be restored because the old values were not saved.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Let heist-granted Black accounts earn interest</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Black accounts granted through heist content can now earn interest without requiring £250 million.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Relentless Bailey now takes belongings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>If rent is two weeks overdue and Bailey catches the player in the street, Bailey can have the bedroom cleared instead of only taking carried cash.</li>
		<li>Taken belongings can be bought back from Bailey's office for one week.</li>
		<li>Paying the rent returns everything normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Bailey, Avery, Gwylan, and starting balance</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bailey's rent checks now count money in the bank when determining whether the Pay option should appear.</li>
		<li>Offering yourself to Bailey no longer clears rent for free when the money is in the bank; Bailey takes the player to HBSC to withdraw it first.</li>
		<li>Avery has a unique response when the player loses a pilled body after using the anti-pill stolen from the HBSC gala.</li>
		<li>Avery's garden scene recognises a freshly harvested garden and gives a Tending S+ compliment.</li>
		<li>Honey challah can now be ordered from Gwylan on the cafe balcony.</li>
		<li><strong>X-Change Purity</strong> now costs 100 coins instead of 150.</li>
		<li>New characters now start with <strong>Mindful</strong> Willpower instead of <strong>Fainthearted</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Autism Spectrum recovery</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sleeping no longer consumes the daily Load recovery allowance.</li>
		<li>Calm time at 0 Load also no longer consumes it.</li>
		<li>Daytime Load recovery can still come from rest, quiet time, and focused interests.</li>
		<li>The daily Load recovery limit increased from 12 to 15.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated reverse rape and Breeder/Omega orgasm rules</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Reverse rape can now trigger regardless of how an enemy is defeated, including counters, escaping grabs, or chastity-gear damage.</li>
		<li>Breeder and Omega characters cannot orgasm without something inside them unless the relevant setting allows it.</li>
		<li>Creampies no longer incorrectly permit every later orgasm until the next bath.</li>
		<li>Forced-orgasm scenes now follow the normal Breeder/Omega denial rules, including Stress and buildup.</li>
		<li>The trait description now reflects the <strong>Allow orgasm without creampie</strong> setting.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Kaiju suits now hide transformation tails</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Water Dragon egg-cycle requirements</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Reproductive checks now require the Water Dragon transformation to be currently manifested.</li>
		<li>Genome Dump immediately clears the egg cycle unless Harper's active lab route is running.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>No X-Change pills while pregnant</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>X-Change transformation pills can no longer be taken during any pregnancy, including normal, anal, parasite, or egg pregnancies.</li>
		<li>This restriction applies to bought pills, drinks, offers, forced pills, and encounter pilling.</li>
		<li>Medicine-drawer pills are disabled with an explanation.</li>
		<li>Unknown pregnancies use vague wording so they are not revealed early.</li>
		<li>Characters who would normally offer or force a pill react differently instead of dosing the player.</li>
		<li>Antidotes and pills that manage an already-active X-Change dose still work.</li>
		<li>X-Change Pink Beta must be taken before pregnancy.</li>
		<li>Existing dual-womb pregnancies continue to work normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Beta second-womb pregnancies</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Named characters and love interests can now cause a second pregnancy through cheat-menu <strong>get pregnant from</strong> options.</li>
		<li>Demon <strong>Force Impregnation</strong> is available whenever a womb is free.</li>
		<li>The anal option still requires no vaginal pregnancy.</li>
		<li>Losing Beta shortly after conception no longer leaves a hidden pregnancy in the removed womb.</li>
		<li>Clearing a pregnancy through cheats also clears Poppy's knowledge of it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pregnancy status and anal conception</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Pregnancy status now clearly shows when another womb or the rear is unavailable because the body is already carrying a pregnancy.</li>
		<li>When both pregnancy readouts are shown, they are labelled <strong>Womb</strong> and <strong>Rear</strong>.</li>
		<li>Anal cum cannot cause pregnancy after Omega ends or while anal pregnancy is disabled.</li>
		<li>Parasite pregnancy text no longer mentions blocking an impossible anal pregnancy.</li>
		<li>Harper's serum is no longer listed as “the father” and instead appears as the cause.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pill restrictions and anal-pregnancy settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>X-Change pills no longer become permanently unavailable after switching away from a previously pregnant body.</li>
		<li>Pills are blocked only by pregnancies that actually conflict with the body they would create.</li>
		<li>Disabled pills now explain whether the problem is body incompatibility, another active pill, pregnancy, or an untested SWP counter-agent.</li>
		<li>Inventory pills show the same explanations.</li>
		<li>NPC spiking now uses the same pill restrictions as voluntary use.</li>
		<li>Anal pregnancy can no longer occur while its setting is disabled, including Fetish mode, Force Impregnation, and named-NPC pregnancies.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed parasite birth and container replacement</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed several combat action and penetration states</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed stale or incorrect anal, vaginal, penis, mouth, hand, and NPC-position states.</li>
		<li>Anal follow-up actions no longer fail or get skipped.</li>
		<li>Hands and mouths now release previous body parts when moving away.</li>
		<li>Pull-out and escape actions use the correct NPC and position.</li>
		<li>Double-penetration escape states are assigned correctly.</li>
		<li>Anal state no longer remains stale after an NPC moves.</li>
		<li>Penis actions no longer switch to incorrect penetration states.</li>
		<li>Mouth penetration states are recognised and repaired correctly.</li>
		<li>Fixed several incorrect states in Kylar and beast scenes.</li>
		<li>Removed duplicated and unused combat handling that could interfere with these actions.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC body parts getting stuck in combat</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>NPC genitals and mouths are now released correctly when actions end.</li>
		<li>Already-stuck body parts repair themselves during combat, including saves made mid-fight.</li>
		<li>Fixed masked kissing mentioning a penis the NPC did not have or interrupting an active penis action.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed combat positions vanishing mid-scene</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Ongoing penetration, grabs, and other occupied positions are no longer incorrectly cleared.</li>
		<li>Covers encounters that begin with penetration already active, submitting during standing fights, losing footing while held by tentacles or critters, choking ending incorrectly, and attackers becoming submissive mid-penetration.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed beast gangbangs after orgasm</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Multi-beast encounters now end correctly.</li>
		<li>Each beast retains its own orgasm progress.</li>
		<li>Group fights no longer duplicate enemies.</li>
		<li>Existing saves that stuck can continue normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed combat speech</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Angel <strong>Forgive</strong>, <strong>Plead</strong>, and <strong>Threaten</strong> no longer trigger jealousy over an unnamed rival.</li>
		<li>Fixed missing Avery and Ivory Wraith responses.</li>
		<li>Love interests without special name-drop dialogue now fall back to normal responses.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Blackmail Club quests getting stuck</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Conclusion letters left unread for seven days now resolve the job automatically.</li>
		<li>Successful jobs still pay out, with a message explaining what happened.</li>
		<li>Added a quest marker and Journal reminder while a conclusion letter is waiting in the bedroom.</li>
		<li>Existing stuck saves resolve automatically after seven in-game days.</li>
		<li>Failed jobs still reset threat progress as before.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed swimsuit locker storage</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Changing swimsuits repeatedly no longer sends the original outfit back to the home wardrobe.</li>
		<li>The player's outfit stays correctly stored in the changing room after swimming lessons.</li>
		<li>Works in both locker rooms and with all body configurations.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed alternate spriteset fallback</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Missing <code>img2</code> sprites now fall back to the normal sprite instead of appearing blank.</li>
		<li>Fixes modded hair and other modded sprites not appearing with the alternate spriteset.</li>
		<li>Prevents mod and embedded image paths from being incorrectly rewritten to <code>img2</code>.</li>
		<li>Missing fallback checks are cached after the first lookup.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed missing clothing sprites and combat image errors</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed duplicated settings and cheat options</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed silent X-Change pill effects</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Unknown pill effects hidden by a passage transition now display a notice on the next passage.</li>
		<li>Added missing drugging/transformation narration for Bailey, the moors abduction, office party, pub, and underwater prison.</li>
		<li>Scenes that already describe the pill or transformation are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin's chest-binder descriptions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Robin is no longer described as wearing a chest binder while gender-flipped.</li>
		<li>Covers room-entry and lemonade-stand scenes, including the scene viewer.</li>
		<li>Other scenes that already handled Robin's X-Changed body correctly are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery date, dinner, and X-Change vow interactions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Removed repeated dialogue and questions during Avery's Valentine's dinner.</li>
		<li>Avery now comments on pregnancy only when they actually intended to give the player a pill.</li>
		<li>Temple-vow forgiveness text now appears only while using a borrowed body.</li>
		<li>Gray and crossdress pills still count as the player's own body.</li>
		<li>Avery's home is now consistently called a mansion in fishing thoughts.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Randomizer settings, talents, and identity</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Random starts no longer create invalid settings that break the Modded Settings page.</li>
		<li>Existing saves with invalid values repair on load.</li>
		<li>Turning off Insanity restores the original talent choices instead of leaving free talents behind.</li>
		<li>Random starts now grant a valid number of talents.</li>
		<li>Random starts no longer create conflicting identity preferences.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed gender being misread while undressing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Characters with both a penis and vagina are no longer automatically read as male when genitals are visible.</li>
		<li>Gender recognition now continues to use overall appearance during undressing and sex.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed clothes tearing and school locker storage</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Accessories, cursed clothing, chastity devices, and unsupported items no longer show <strong>Tear</strong>.</li>
		<li>School pool locker clothing no longer disappears when <strong>Multiple wardrobes</strong> is disabled.</li>
		<li>Clothing already stuck there is moved to the orphanage wardrobe when loading a save.</li>
		<li>Separate wardrobes such as Eden's cabin and the farm remain separate.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed lost NPC state after stimming</strong> after Police Molestation.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed temple Innocence-pill issues</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed an error when receiving the Innocence pill with Sydney.</li>
		<li>Added the missing Innocence-pill atonement in confession after both temple vows are broken.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed tanning lines from clothing</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed blackmail edge cases</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gentleman's Club blackmail tasks are cancelled when a soft bad end prevents completion, including farm, asylum, prison, pound, wolf cave, Eden, Kylar, and mines.</li>
		<li>The blackmail remains active and a new task arrives a few days after returning.</li>
		<li>Tasks already waiting for a reply letter are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed fishing-related UI</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The sidebar drunk indicator now changes colour with drunkenness instead of always appearing red.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</span> Art and Graphics</h2>
